VeridianOS: install.texi: list the top-level nodes in document order

makeinfo (texinfo 7.3) reported, building gccinstall.info:

  install.texi:116: warning: node next pointer for `Installing GCC' is
    `Binaries' but next is `Specific' in menu
  install.texi:116: warning: node prev pointer for `Specific' is
    `Binaries' but prev is `Installing GCC' in menu
  install.texi:117: warning: node next pointer for `Specific' is
    `GNU Free Documentation License' but next is `Binaries' in menu
  install.texi:117: warning: node prev pointer for `Binaries' is
    `Installing GCC' but prev is `Specific' in menu
  install.texi:119: warning: node next pointer for `Binaries' is
    `Specific' but next is `GNU Free Documentation License' in menu
  install.texi:119: warning: node prev pointer for `GNU Free
    Documentation License' is `Specific' but prev is `Binaries' in menu

The nodes are in the order Installing GCC, Binaries, Specific, GNU Free
Documentation License, and their explicit Next/Prev pointers (including
the one in include/fdl.texi) follow that order; only the Top menu listed
Specific before Binaries.  The menu now lists them in document order.
The generated gccinstall.info differs only in the order of those two
Top menu entries.

diff -ru a/gcc/doc/install.texi b/gcc/doc/install.texi
--- a/gcc/doc/install.texi	2026-08-07 03:46:06.125689311 -0400
+++ b/gcc/doc/install.texi	2026-10-08 17:05:54.029676277 -0400
@@ -113,8 +113,8 @@
                     procedure for GCC as well as detailing some target
                     specific installation instructions.
 
-* Specific::        Host/target specific installation notes for GCC.
 * Binaries::        Where to get pre-compiled binaries.
+* Specific::        Host/target specific installation notes for GCC.
 
 * GNU Free Documentation License:: How you can copy and share this manual.
 * Concept Index::   This index has two entries.
